                <pb facs="1293" n="1252" sameAs="frus:frus1949v03/pg1252"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On November 17 the National Security Council submitted to President
                        Truman
                    NSC 38/4 on the future courses of United States
                    action with respect to Austria. This paper <hi rendition="#italic">inter
                        alia</hi> analyzed the problem of Austrian internal security in terms of the
                    formation of an Austrian Army. The conclusions of the paper were then approved
                    by President Truman and its implementation was to be
                    coordinated by the Secretary of State. For the text of NSC 38/4, see <ref target="#pg1190">page 1190</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
